From 05749a111ae04684d5b1e10658f37f5d5dc640bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:07:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau: do not claim DRIVER_ATOMIC without an
 atomic_commit

nouveau.atomic=1 sets DRIVER_ATOMIC on the shared driver struct before any
device exists (nouveau_drm.c:882), so it applies to every nouveau card in the
machine. Only nv50+ display installs atomic mode_config funcs
(dispnv50/disp.c:2847); a card with no outp_mask and no DCB entries never
creates a display at all and keeps nouveau_mode_config_funcs, which carries
.fb_create and nothing else -- ->atomic_commit is NULL.

drm_drv_uses_atomic_modeset() returns true on the feature flag alone
(drm_drv.h:563), so the fbdev client takes the atomic path and
drm_atomic_commit() calls that NULL pointer. On a hybrid laptop, where the
discrete GPU is a 3D controller with no display engine, it oopses during probe
before anything is mounted:

    drm_atomic_commit+0xbe/0xe0
    drm_client_modeset_commit_atomic+0x19b/0x230
    drm_client_modeset_commit+0x22/0x40
    drm_fbdev_client_hotplug+0x66/0xb0
    drm_client_register+0x6a/0xb0
    drm_fbdev_client_setup+0xad/0x1b0
    nouveau_drm_probe+0x15d/0x170
    RIP: 0010:0x0

driver_features is a per-device mask ANDed with the driver's (drm_drv.h:532)
and starts as ~0u (drm_drv.c:726), so clearing it after display creation
disables atomic for this card alone. A second nouveau card that did install an
atomic_commit keeps it -- which matters, because on a desktop where nouveau
drives the monitor drm_hwcomposer requires DRM_CLIENT_CAP_ATOMIC and cannot
run without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GyZRNL2xBh9BWrNiQX2Hsh
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c
index d71dcfc6ee66..22fcf3a373b3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c
@@ -710,6 +710,34 @@ nouveau_display_create(struct drm_device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto disp_create_err;
 
+	/* Do not claim DRIVER_ATOMIC on a device that installed no atomic_commit.
+	 *
+	 * nouveau.atomic=1 sets DRIVER_ATOMIC on the shared driver struct before
+	 * any device exists (nouveau_drm.c), so it lands on every nouveau card in
+	 * the machine. Only nv50+ display installs atomic funcs (dispnv50/disp.c);
+	 * a card that reaches the else-branch above -- no outp_mask and no DCB
+	 * entries -- keeps nouveau_mode_config_funcs, which has fb_create and
+	 * nothing else.
+	 *
+	 * drm_drv_uses_atomic_modeset() then returns true purely on the feature
+	 * flag (drm_drv.h:563), so the fbdev client takes the atomic path and
+	 * drm_atomic_commit() calls a NULL ->atomic_commit. On a hybrid laptop,
+	 * where the discrete GPU is a 3D controller with no display engine, that
+	 * is an oops during probe before anything is mounted:
+	 *
+	 *     drm_atomic_commit+0xbe/0xe0
+	 *     drm_client_modeset_commit_atomic+0x19b/0x230
+	 *     drm_fbdev_client_hotplug+0x66/0xb0
+	 *     nouveau_drm_probe+0x15d/0x170
+	 *     RIP: 0010:0x0
+	 *
+	 * driver_features is a per-device MASK ANDed with the driver's
+	 * (drm_drv.h:532), so clearing it here disables atomic for this card only
+	 * and leaves a second, display-capable nouveau card untouched.
+	 */
+	if (!dev->mode_config.funcs->atomic_commit)
+		dev->driver_features &= ~DRIVER_ATOMIC;
+
 	drm_mode_config_reset(dev);
 
 	if (dev->mode_config.num_crtc) {
-- 
